WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.480
Imagine a screening clinic with a limited testing budget. The practical question is simple.

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:09.480
Which numbers are reliable enough to decide who should receive further testing?

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:15.480
The data set also needs one correction before any result is interpreted.

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:23.920
Smith and colleagues explain on pages 261 to 262 that the study forecast the onset

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:31.440
of diabetes within 5 years among women who did not have diabetes at baseline. Outcome therefore

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:38.080
represents 5-year onset, not a diagnosis already present when the predictors were measured.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:45.280
I applied one test throughout. Would I trust this number at the clinic?

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:53.400
My conclusion is that two impressive numbers borrowed their strength from how the data

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:59.720
were collected. While glucose earned its strength through real 5-year prediction.
